  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "remove-thread-ownership-check",
      "title": "Remove per-endpoint thread ownership (user_id) authorization checks from run-creation endpoints",
      "rationale": "All four hunks delete the same inline `existing_thread.user_id != user.identity` guard (and its now-unused ThreadORM import) from the create/stream/wait run endpoints, so they collectively change one access-control concern: whether thread ownership is enforced before run creation.",
      "hunks": [
        "libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/api/runs.py#0",
        "libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/api/runs.py#1",
        "libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/api/runs.py#2",
        "libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/api/runs.py#3"
      ],
      "context": [
        {"path": "libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/services/run_preparation.py", "symbol": "_prepare_run", "start_line": 160, "end_line": 278, "snapshot": "base", "why": "Downstream shared helper called by all three endpoints; does not itself verify thread.user_id ownership, so removing the inline check leaves no ownership enforcement on the create/stream/wait paths."},
        {"path": "libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/services/run_preparation.py", "symbol": "update_thread_metadata", "start_line": 103, "end_line": 157, "snapshot": "base", "why": "Auto-creates or updates a thread without checking existing thread.user_id, so a removed guard would let a user act on another user's thread."},
        {"path": "libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/core/auth_handlers.py", "symbol": "handle_event", "start_line": 62, "end_line": 158, "snapshot": "base", "why": "The only remaining authorization hook (create_run on threads) is opt-in and defaults to allow when no handler is configured, so it does not substitute for the removed ownership check."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "cwe_id": "CWE-639",
      "explanation": "The PR removes the inline thread-ownership check from all three run-creation endpoints (create_run, create_and_stream_run, wait_for_run). The removed guard verified `existing_thread.user_id != user.identity` and raised 404, preventing a user from creating a run on another user's thread. The only remaining authorization hook, `handle_event` (auth_handlers.py:62-158), is explicitly opt-in and 'allows by default' when no auth instance or handler is configured (lines 108-122), so it does not enforce ownership. The downstream shared helper `_prepare_run` (run_preparation.py:160-278) and `update_thread_metadata` (run_preparation.py:103-157) do not verify `thread.user_id` ownership — `update_thread_metadata` even auto-creates a thread with the caller's user_id and updates an existing thread's metadata without checking the existing owner. Consequently, after this change any authenticated user can act on (create runs against, and mutate metadata of) a thread owned by another user via the user-controlled `thread_id` path parameter.",
      "evidence": [
        {"type": "code", "file": "libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/api/runs.py", "lines": [53, 56], "content": "    # Authorization check (create_run action on threads resource)
    ctx = build_auth_context(user, "threads", "create_run")
    value = {**request.model_dump(), "thread_id": thread_id}
    filters = await handle_event(ctx, value)"},
        {"type": "code", "file": "libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/api/runs.py", "lines": [95, 95], "content": "    run_id, run, _job = await _prepare_run(session, thread_id, request, user, initial_status="pending")"},
        {"type": "code", "file": "libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/core/auth_handlers.py", "lines": [108, 122], "content": "    auth = get_auth_instance()
    if auth is None:
        # No auth configured, allow by default
        return None
    ...
    handler = _get_handler(auth, auth_ctx.resource, auth_ctx.action)
    if handler is None:
        # No handler for this resource/action, allow by default
        return None"},
        {"type": "code", "file": "libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/services/run_preparation.py", "lines": [120, 143], "content": "    thread = await session.scalar(select(ThreadORM).where(ThreadORM.thread_id == thread_id))
    ...
    if not thread:
        # Auto-create thread if it doesn't exist
        ...
        thread_orm = ThreadORM(thread_id=thread_id, status="idle", metadata_json=metadata, user_id=user_id)
        session.add(thread_orm)
        return"},
        {"type": "policy", "source": "libs/aegra-api/tests/e2e/manual_auth_tests/README.md", "content": "These tests verify the authentication and authorization functionality of Aegra. Since Aegra is designed to be a package where users implement their own auth, these tests are not part of the regular test suite."}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Restore the thread-ownership verification in each endpoint (or centralize it in `_prepare_run`/`update_thread_metadata`) so that a 404/403 is raised when `existing_thread.user_id != user.identity`. Do not rely solely on the opt-in `handle_event` hook, which defaults to allow when no handler is configured.",
      "file": "libs/aegra-api/src/aegra_api/api/runs.py",
      "line": 53
    }
  ]
}

